1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,050
This video shows how a clinician edits the INR in place, inside the consultation form.

2
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:14,553
In ACT 2.0, a button under the chart opened the INR monitoring form. Here the clinician edits it without leaving the consultation.

3
00:00:16,153 --> 00:00:25,965
This test patient has three INR results and an active visit. Under Consultation visits, Start consultation opens the RHD Consultation Visit form.

4
00:00:27,273 --> 00:00:40,140
I maximize the workspace and scroll to Cardiac medications. The latest INR is 2.6, on the twelfth of October. Under the chart are two buttons, Edit INR monitoring and Record new INR.

5
00:00:41,553 --> 00:00:46,373
First I type a sentence into Interval History. That is the consultation's own text.

6
00:00:47,113 --> 00:00:54,849
Now I click Edit INR monitoring. The panel opens under the chart. The consultation, and the text I typed, stay where they are.

7
00:00:55,993 --> 00:01:02,181
The panel holds the date tested, the INR value, the dose change, the target, and the next INR date.

8
00:01:03,753 --> 00:01:12,044
I change the INR value from 2.6 to 3.1, and press Save. The chart updates at once, and the typed text is still there.

9
00:01:14,553 --> 00:01:22,078
This edit is saved straight away, apart from the consultation's own Save. So I cancel the consultation, and the edit stays.

10
00:01:24,078 --> 00:01:30,804
Here is a new consultation for the same patient. The edit survived. The latest INR now reads 3.1.

11
00:01:39,398 --> 00:01:46,286
Now Record new INR. The same panel opens in a second mode. The target is taken from the latest entry.

12
00:01:47,598 --> 00:01:54,717
I enter an INR of 2.4, and press Save. This saves a new INR Monitoring record, and the chart gains a point.

13
00:01:56,717 --> 00:02:01,757
Now the checks. I open Edit INR monitoring and type an INR of 100.

14
00:02:10,077 --> 00:02:16,524
Save shows a message. It asks for an INR above 0, and up to 99. Nothing is written.

15
00:02:17,517 --> 00:02:21,826
Cancel closes the panel without writing anything. Escape does the same.

16
00:02:23,957 --> 00:02:34,305
Pressing Enter in the panel does not save the consultation. I press Enter in the INR field. The panel stays open, the consultation form is still open, and nothing was saved.

17
00:02:36,305 --> 00:02:42,496
It writes the whole entry. The form engine's own edit lost the date tested. This editor avoids that.

18
00:02:43,196 --> 00:02:48,490
An entry that shares its target and next INR date with earlier entries shows them read only.

19
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:57,052
The clinician and the site administrator see it. It needs the INR chart, pull request 224, first.

20
00:02:57,752 --> 00:03:02,709
The agreed warfarin target range, A R 124, is still open.

21
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:13,959
Three pull requests, in order. ACT app 224, the chart. ACT app 227, this editor. And distro 300, the form question.

22
00:03:14,659 --> 00:03:19,582
The old button, pull request 225, is closed in favour of this editor.
